; PlayQuake -- GLQuake on the Radeon through RadeonGL, with sound and LAN
; play, at the fastest RadeonGL settings (README.md beside this script):
;   RadeonGLCheck 0    the command check off
;   RadeonGLDirect 1   the vertex stream straight into video RAM
;   -lm_LUMINANCE      8-bit lightmaps (id's own default)
;   320 x 240          GLQuake's default screen
; Sound: Paula through GLQuake's own DMA driver; for AHI add -ahi below.
; LAN: UDP through the running TCP/IP stack's bsdsocket.library.
; Put it in the GLQuake drawer, beside glquake and id1, and double-click
; it, or CD there and Execute PlayQuake. Anything after the name goes to
; GLQuake as well:  Execute PlayQuake +timedemo demo1
.KEY ARGS/F
.BRA {
.KET }
FailAt 21
Stack 1000000
Set RadeonGLCheck 0
Set RadeonGLDirect 1
glquake -nocdaudio -lm_LUMINANCE {ARGS}
UnSet RadeonGLCheck
UnSet RadeonGLDirect
